---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="A bit about who's writing here and what to expect."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-05-27')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Parker. I'm a software engineer who spends a lot of time these days at the
		intersection of code and AI — building tools that compose models with the rest of a system,
		automating the boring stuff, and occasionally tearing apart public software to understand
		how it really works.
	</p>

	<p>
		This blog is where I write down what I learn while building. Posts tend to be one of:
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Build logs</strong> — what I made, why the shape ended up the way it did, what didn't work first.</li>
		<li><strong>Investigations</strong> — pulling on a thread until I understand a system or a failure mode.</li>
		<li><strong>Tooling notes</strong> — small posts about useful patterns, weird gotchas, and things I want to remember.</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		Code for most of what I write about is on
		<a href="https://github.com/psoren" rel="me">GitHub @psoren</a>. The source for the blog
		itself is at
		<a href="https://github.com/psoren/psoren-blog">github.com/psoren/psoren-blog</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
